# NOTIS AI AGENT SYSTEM RULES (.cursorrules)
# Version: 1.0.0 (September 2026)
# Target Stack: Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, Prisma 6, Neon PostgreSQL, Tailwind v4, Zod, @xyflow/react

# ==============================================================================
# 0. CRITICAL MANDATORY INVARIANT
# ==============================================================================
# BEFORE PERFORMING ANY TASK OR WRITING ANY CODE:
# 1. You MUST read and strictly adhere to "docs/ARCHITECTURE_RULES.md".
# 2. You MUST check the current task queue and acceptance criteria in "docs/TASK_QUEUE.md".
# 3. You MUST NEVER bypass architectural guidelines, introduce one-off hardcoded hacks,
#    or break existing test suites.

# ==============================================================================
# 1. ARCHITECTURAL PATTERNS & PROHIBITIONS
# ==============================================================================
# [QUIZ ENGINE: STRICT PROHIBITION OF HARDCODING]
# - NEVER hardcode question types with scattered if/switch checks in components or services.
# - The Quiz Engine strictly follows the polymorphic Strategy / Registry pattern.
# - Supported types: SINGLE_CHOICE, MULTIPLE_CHOICE, SHORT_ANSWER, CODE, FLASHCARD.
# - Every question type must provide:
#     a) Zod configuration & answer schema
#     b) Server-side pure Evaluator (zero-trust, isolated from answer leakage)
#     c) Client-side interactive Input component registered in the UI factory
#     d) Authoring Studio Form in the drawer (/studio/[slug])
# - Never implement one question type in isolation if it breaks or bypasses the registry contract.

# [MUTATIONS & SAFE ACTIONS (RESULT PATTERN)]
# - All mutations must be encapsulated in "createSafeAction".
# - NEVER throw unhandled errors to the client.
# - Always validate raw input using Zod before executing business logic.
# - Use "ActionException(code, message)" for expected domain errors (UNAUTHORIZED, FORBIDDEN, BAD_REQUEST, CONFLICT, NOT_FOUND).
# - Obfuscate unexpected database/runtime crashes into INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR.
# - Always rethrow Next.js framework system errors (NEXT_REDIRECT, NEXT_NOT_FOUND).

# [ZERO-TRUST SECURITY]
# - NEVER leak correct answers, regex patterns, or hidden code test cases to client DTOs.
# - Answers are verified strictly on the server.
# - Explanations and answer evaluations are returned only after submission is graded.
# - Anti-exploit: XP is granted only once on first completion. Re-takes strictly yield 0 XP.

# [DATABASE INTEGRITY & TRANSACTIONS]
# - Foreign keys follow "onDelete: Restrict" semantics.
# - NEVER perform single-row ad-hoc deletions of parent entities (Course, Topic, Question, User).
# - Complex deletions MUST run inside "prisma.$transaction" with explicit cleanup of dependent records:
#     prerequisites, graph layouts, quiz attempts, review cards, translations, and user progress.

# [ROADMAP GRAPH & DFS CYCLE GUARD]
# - The roadmap graph is strictly a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG).
# - Adding any edge (TopicPrerequisite) MUST pass DFS cycle detection via "wouldCreateCycle".
# - Reject self-loops and any transitive paths that create cycles with CONFLICT error.
# - Respect Course Tiers and deterministic Fog of War calculations (LOCKED, AVAILABLE, IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETED).

# [SPACED REPETITION (SM-2)]
# - SuperMemo-2 mathematical formulas for Easiness Factor (EF) and intervals (I) are invariant.
# - Support automatic card ingestion (completed topics) and manual cards (Flashcard Builder).

# ==============================================================================
# 2. QUALITY GATES & VERIFICATION (ZERO-REGRESSION POLICY)
# ==============================================================================
# - Before reporting task completion, you MUST run:
#     pnpm validate (runs: pnpm typecheck && pnpm test && pnpm build)
# - All existing 185+ tests MUST remain 100% passing.
# - Any new logic or Server Action MUST include corresponding unit tests covering both
#   valid input and boundary/error conditions.
# - Update "docs/TASK_QUEUE.md" to reflect current progress upon completion.
